kbase: dump the native swapchain BOs of the real image size

The bring-up dump only inspected 640x480x4 BOs, so on a session whose
swapchain images are 1600x720 (4608000 bytes) it never printed the
guest's own view of the buffer the compositor samples.  Widen the filter
to the swapchain size actually in use so the guest-side ground truth
exists.

diff --git a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
index 09caa7d..f558d55 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
@@ -1663,11 +1663,13 @@ kbase_kmod_debug_dump_native_bos(struct pan_kmod_dev *dev)
       uint64_t size = kbase_dev->debug_bo_sizes[i];
 
       /*
-       * PANVKDBG: only touch the 640x480x4 native swapchain-image BOs.
-       * Large grow-on-fault/heap mappings can SIGBUS on CPU access when
-       * pages are not committed.
+       * PANVKDBG: only touch the native swapchain-image BOs.  Large
+       * grow-on-fault/heap mappings can SIGBUS on CPU access when pages are
+       * not committed, so skip anything that is not one of the known
+       * swapchain image sizes.
        */
-      if (!p || size != 640ull * 480ull * 4ull)
+      if (!p || (size != 640ull * 480ull * 4ull &&
+                 size != 1600ull * 720ull * 4ull))
          continue;
 
       /*
